 for all $t>0.$\nNext, we solve for $T(t),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T-34 & ={e}^{-0.07t+C} \\\\ T-34 & ={e}^{C}{e}^{-0.07t} \\\\ T-34 & =K{e}^{-0.07t} \\\\ T & =34+K{e}^{-0.07t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $K={e}^{C}$ is a constant of integration. \n\nWe're told that the initial temperature of the bulb was ${65}^{∘}C.$ So, we apply the initial condition $T(0)=65,$ and solve for $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}65 & =34+K{e}^{0} \\\\ 65 & =34+K \\\\ K & =31\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to our initial value problem is\n\n$$\nT(t)=34+31{e}^{-0.07t}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the temperature of the bulb after $t=7$ minutes is\n\n$$\nT(7)=34+31{e}^{-0.07\\cdot 7}≈{53}^{∘}\\text{C},\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer." 13194139538705 17592186045443 true] [17592186672759 1075 #edb/ref 17592186672732 13194139538705 17592186045443 true] [17592186672759 1075 #edb/ref 17592186672742 13194139538705 17592186045443 true] [17592186672759 1075 #edb/ref 17592186672761 13194139538705 17592186045443 true] [17592186672759 1075 #edb/ref 17592186672764 13194139538705 17592186045443 true] [17592186672759 1075 #edb/ref 17592186672765 13194139538705 17592186045443 true] [17592186672759 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139538705 17592186045443 true] [17592186672759 1077 "selection" 13194139538705 17592186045443 true] [17592186672759 1078 #edb/ref 17592186672742 13194139538705 17592186045443 true] [17592186672759 1079 #uuid "9b78b1b8-fbe7-50fe-a450-31525c7b8ea4" 13194139538705 17592186045443 true] [17592186672760 1075 #edb/ref 17592186672733 13194139538705 17592186045443 true] [17592186672760 1075 #edb/ref 17592186672743 13194139538705 17592186045443 true] [17592186672760 1075 #edb/ref 17592186672749 13194139538705 17592186045443 true] [17592186672760 1075 #edb/ref 17592186672753 13194139538705 17592186045443 true] [17592186672760 1075 #edb/ref 17592186672756 13194139538705 17592186045443 true] [17592186672760 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139538705 17592186045443 true]